  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-PS Youth in Civic Space Participation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under this project PNGO will work closely with the selected youth organizations  under the sub granting scheme to develop communitymobilization and outreach strategies, thereby enhancing inclusivity and creating community protection mechanisms and toolsto eventually develop two comprehensive strategies (one in the West Bank and one in Gaza strip). PNGO and Oxfam will facilitate multiple learning and exchange sessions, encouraging youth organizations and their groups to collectively address their challenges and collaboratively strategize solutions. To ensure that Palestinian youth organizations/networks are supported and capacitated towards promoting collective action on critical youth-related human and legal rights topics in oPt CSOs, a series of coaching activities will be provided by Oxfam, PNGO and AIDA  including youth-friendly and gender focused training sessions and the provision of tools such as feminist leadership, youth-tailored influencing approaches, Community-Led Action Planning (CALP), digital security, safeguarding, aid obstruction, shrinking space and counter terrorism. To ensure the long-term sustainability of legal and protection services, PNGO will establish standardized operation procedures (SOPs), encompassing both direct service delivery and referrals to individual services, the SOPs will be targeting youth activities and youth based CSOs and will be disseminated through the subgrantees and PNGO members. Based on the consultations with the target groups/organizations, PNGO and Oxfamwill collaborate to design strategic interventions aimed at enhancing the overall well-being of youth advocates, activists, and human rights defenders. These interventions will encompassboth individual and collective well-being initiatives, ensuring thatthe physical and mental health of youth engaged in advocating for their rights is adequately supported and nurtured.
To maintain the relevance and strategic focus of the project, partners will invest in a continuous dialogue between youth organizationsand the project partners. Regular meetings and discussions will be organized and will play a key role in shaping the project&apos;s strategies and ensuring that the implementation processes remain responsive to the challenges and opportunities faced by youthandyoung women in particular. Project partners will seek partnerships and alliances  with reputable regional and international entities such as the digital rights coalitions, SMEX, Access Now and the Citizen Lab as well as Digital Rights Coalition that havevaluable expertise in digital rights advocacy and gender justice. To maximize the impact of the advocacy efforts, AIDA and PNGO will establish a consistent and continuous channel of communication between AIDA and PNGOs task force that will serve as an avenue for enhanced advocacy efforts. Through joint initiatives and coordinated advocacy campaigns implemented as a part of the complementary Pathways of change, project partners and targeted youth groups/entities will work collectively to influence policy changes. To further foster collaboration and knowledge exchange, a dedicated platform will be established that links youth organizations in the West Bank and Gaza with regional youth activists and networks.
PNGO will conduct comprehensive analysis onexisting laws and policies that directly affect CSOs and youth organizations in the oPt. This analysis will include key legislation, including cybercrime law, law of nor chartable society the law of nonprofit companies. To raise awareness, inform policy advocacy, and inspire collective action, series of case studies will be developed/compiled by PNGO that highlight thematic issues from the perspective of youth activists, youth-based organizations, informal groups, young journalists, influencers, and movements. PNGO, in partnership with OXFAM, will work collectively to support development and implementation of unified campaign and advocacy strategy, harnessing the expertise and creativity of youth leaders (mainly the subgrantees and their youth groups) ona predefined common cause around shrinking of civic space. To reach wider audience, nationally and internally, AIDA and PNGO will develop and disseminate joint press releases, statements and position papers on aid obstruction and shrinking space issues, includingCTL. Finally, both AIDA
and PNGO will organize at least one international mission per year and yearly event/conference where AIDA will disseminate legal brief on shrinking civic space and CTL impact on humanitarian space.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OXFAM-IN-BELGIUM (SOLIDARIT&#xc9;)</narrative>
  </participating-org>
  <participating-org ref="NL-KVK-27108436" role="4" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Novib has been active in the Occupied Palestinian Territory/Israel (OPT/I) since 1982 and working with Palestinian refugees in Lebanon since the mid 1980s. It has built up a strong network of relationships with local NGOs and counts among its localcounterparts some of the largest and most professional NGOs in various sectors. It has accompanied these NGOs in their development from ad hoc volunteer groups to sizeable professional institutions with national outreach.  At the same time the conceptualisation of the programme has evolved from three country programs in the early 1990s to a program for Palestinians in the Middle East (PME) working withPalestinians in OPT, Israel and Lebanon.

The programme has changed over the years with the establishment of the Palestinian Authority (PA) in the mid-1990s from a focus on support and service provision at a grassroots level and grassroots mobilization, to working towards influencing the establishment of the PA, its lawmaking and supporting building a democratic state # this involved supporting efforts of Palestinian civil society to build the basis for a democratic Palestinian state with room for civil participation, ensuring inclusion of vulnerable groups, refugees and women, and shaping its laws and systems. Oxfam Novib has also supported partners that are working on the provision of humanitarian assistance, response preparedness and conflict transformation. We have also supported partners in the provision of health services, access to quality education and gender justice.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Novib</narrative>
